  "result": "Excellent! All 62 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Created src/numbering.js:**\n- `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` \u2014 generates invoice numbers in format `INV-YYYY-CCCC` where:\n  - `YYYY` is the year extracted from the issueDate\n  - `CCCC` is a 4-digit zero-padded counter starting at 0001 for each year\n  - Resets to 0001 each year, ignoring invoices from other years\n\n**Added to src/invoices.js:**\n- `issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)` \u2014 converts a draft invoice to issued:\n  - Validates the invoice is in draft status (returns `NOT_DRAFT` if not)\n  - Assigns the next invoice number using `nextInvoiceNumber`\n  - Sets status to `'issued'`\n  - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the number field added\n  - Does not mutate the input invoice\n  - Returns copies of all line data to prevent external mutation\n\n**Tests added:**\n- **numbering.test.js** (7 tests): first invoice of year, counter increment, unordered lists, year filtering, 4-digit padding, large counters, year extraction\n- **invoices.test.js** (6 new tests): number assignment, number generation from existing, multi-year handling, NOT_DRAFT error, immutability, line copying\n\nThe numbering system handles edge cases like:\n- Multiple years in the existing numbers list\n- Unordered invoice numbers\n- Counters exceeding 9999 (generates 10000+ if needed)\n- New years starting fresh at 0001",
